SYNTHESIS
  In the factorial-origin basis, Q0 is literally even-support minus
  odd-support.  The exact evidence supports an odd-support L1 envelope,
  not a naive signed odd cone: aggregate odd_L1 is larger, but most
  negative Product-Actual rows are signed-even-led after cancellation.
  The positive-Q0 exceptions are useful, not noise: they are the rows where
  odd support wins in the signed aggregate and flips the origin atom.
  A plausible proof target is therefore an odd-support envelope plus a
  finite ledger for signed-even-led low-height packets, followed by the
  HYP-2717 high-height tail estimate for the remaining origin atom.
